=========================================================================================================
20_moleculeace_prepare.py — MoleculeACE targets for the generalization benchmark
=========================================================================================================

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] What this step does
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Converts the MoleculeACE bioactivity sets with at most 1000 compounds into the format the
  pipeline         reads (cid, Smiles, Standard Value, pIC50 Value), one CSV per target. Their
  potency column is already the         negative logarithm of a molar concentration (pKi or
  pEC50), the same scale as the pIC50 of the main benchmark,         so no transformation is
  applied and no value is recomputed.
  The predefined 80/20 split and the activity-cliff flag of each compound are written next to each
  data set, so         that the benchmark can be scored both on our own nested cross-validation
  and on the partition the original         authors published, and so that the error on cliff
  compounds can be reported separately.
